  "structural_law": "In a high-filler atom xP+c=q m with c in R_x, the cofactor m is an x-rough integer in (x,P). If x>=sqrt(P), this forces m to be prime, so the carry shell is a genuine prime-pair shell. Composite cofactors can occur only in the early band x<sqrt(P), and then their prime factors are all >x, giving a finite recursive depth bounded by log P/log x. Persistent recursive concentration is a PDEC object; sparse recursive escape is SAE/LocalSurvivor.",
  "terminal_gap_after_router": "PrimePairCarryShellCapacityAndCompositeCofactorDepthDescent",
  "terminal_gap_expansion": [
    "PrimePairCarryShellCapacityBoundOrPDECReturn",
    "CompositeCofactorDepthDescentOrNamedReturn",
    "EarlyBandLocalSurvivorOrSAEExclusion"
  ]
